    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "K2wFC",
      "x": 28560,
      "y": 1977,
      "name": "07 Interaction and implementation notes",
      "clip": true,
      "width": 1440,
      "fill": "$md-bg",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 28,
      "padding": 48,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "LXipa",
          "name": "Notes title",
          "fill": "$md-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "One business. One clear next step.",
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "fontFamily": "$md-font",
          "fontSize": 36,
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "HPNAT",
          "name": "Interaction destinations",
          "fill": "$md-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Interaction destinations",
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "fontFamily": "$md-font",
          "fontSize": 22,
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "tXRGN",
          "name": "Interaction destinations body",
          "fill": "$md-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "The tool schema exposes editable layers and context, but no prototype transition API. Buttons carry destination/action annotations in their layer context. Follow the flow order below and named frames. These screens are design states, not a connected ERPNext application.",
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "fontFamily": "$md-font",
          "fontSize": 16,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "R7shv",
          "name": "Quick sale routes",
          "fill": "$md-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Quick sale routes",
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "fontFamily": "$md-font",
          "fontSize": 22,
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "oAncJ",
          "name": "Quick sale routes body",
          "fill": "$md-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Home / Sell → Quick sale 01 Customer → 02 Items → 03 Basket → 04 Review and payment → 05 Receipt.\nAdd customer → Quick customer → return to current basket.\nPrice & discount → Price and discount → apply to basket.\nStock unavailable → Insufficient stock → reduce quantity or select warehouse.\nTimeout after confirm → Unresolved → Check result → found: Receipt; pending: stay unresolved; definitively failed: preserved review.",
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "fontFamily": "$md-font",
          "fontSize": 16,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "PNPTp",
          "name": "Connection routes",
          "fill": "$md-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Connection routes",
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "fontFamily": "$md-font",
          "fontSize": 22,
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "Dklav",
          "name": "Connection routes body",
          "fill": "$md-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Connect business → Sign in → Home. Invitation resolves business before sign-in. Connected businesses → choose workspace. Switching during editing → Save draft & switch or Stay in sale. Saved draft stays in the original business. Session recovery returns to that business and draft.",
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "fontFamily": "$md-font",
          "fontSize": 16,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "BejQA",
          "name": "Responsive and platform behavior",
          "fill": "$md-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Responsive and platform behavior",
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "fontFamily": "$md-font",
          "fontSize": 22,
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "USqsf",
          "name": "Responsive and platform behavior body",
          "fill": "$md-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Android: native system back follows the current task; back during editing offers Save draft / Keep editing. iOS: safe-area inset and system share sheet; swipe-back follows the same unsaved guard. Mobile browser: address-bar changes never cover bottom actions; browser Back preserves task state and invokes the guard.\n320–389 px: stack action pairs and form columns; labels wrap; never cut amounts. 768–1199 px: collapsible navigation rail and stacked task panels. 1200+ px: full sidebar, searchable tables and persistent detail/basket panels. Screen frames show full scroll content; production mobile pins task actions above safe area.",
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "fontFamily": "$md-font",
          "fontSize": 16,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "gZcsD",
          "name": "Keyboard and access",
          "fill": "$md-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Keyboard and access",
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "fontFamily": "$md-font",
          "fontSize": 22,
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "zuLim",
          "name": "Keyboard and access body",
          "fill": "$md-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Tab order follows reading order; visible 2 px teal focus ring. Enter selects a highlighted search result. Escape closes a selector without losing data. No shortcut finalizes a transaction without explicit review. Screen-reader labels include field name, currency, quantity, and status. Use text labels with colors.",
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "fontFamily": "$md-font",
          "fontSize": 16,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "V6NnpD",
          "name": "Drafts, permissions and isolation",
          "fill": "$md-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Drafts, permissions and isolation",
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "fontFamily": "$md-font",
          "fontSize": 22,
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "JfpNQ",
          "name": "Drafts, permissions and isolation body",
          "fill": "$md-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Save draft never finalizes invoices, payments or stock. Draft lists and pending confirmations belong to the active business. During loss of connection, retain task state and block confirmation. Do not imply offline completed transactions or synchronization. Server addresses only appear in connection setup/settings.\nCost visibility, price overrides, walk-in use, and module access depend on permissions. Hide inaccessible navigation; show a clear reason when an otherwise relevant action is blocked.",
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "fontFamily": "$md-font",
          "fontSize": 16,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "EpbyP",
          "name": "Sample arithmetic and actions",
          "fill": "$md-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Sample arithmetic and actions",
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "fontFamily": "$md-font",
          "fontSize": 22,
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "oYhwc",
          "name": "Sample arithmetic and actions body",
          "fill": "$md-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Quick sale: 2 trees × ILS 85 + consultation ILS 150 = ILS 320. Partial receipt ILS 120 leaves ILS 200. Supply now explicitly delivers only the 2 stocked items. Service completion remains unrecorded. No taxes or discounts in sample; production totals follow the active business settings.\nPurchase: 10 × 45 = 450 ordered; 6 received and invoiced = 270; payment 100 leaves invoice balance 170. Remaining 4 units / 180 are an unreceived commitment, not an invoice debt.\nProject: 12 needed; supply 8, buy 4. Delivering to site does not consume materials. Consumption and unused returns have separate confirmations.",
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "fontFamily": "$md-font",
          "fontSize": 16,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "VVnw2",
          "name": "Status model",
          "fill": "$md-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Status model",
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "fontFamily": "$md-font",
          "fontSize": 22,
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "ZkIhA",
          "name": "Status model body",
          "fill": "$md-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Keep document, payment and delivery labels separate. A confirmed invoice can be partially paid and partially delivered. Mark unresolved confirmation explicitly. If a result is uncertain, retain its operation reference and check before offering another attempt.",
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "fontFamily": "$md-font",
          "fontSize": 16,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "LVvOi",
          "name": "Product scope",
          "fill": "$md-ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Product scope",
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "fontFamily": "$md-font",
          "fontSize": 22,
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "Hud0x",
          "name": "Product scope body",
          "fill": "$md-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "One operating company per connection. ILS is the primary sample currency; formatting and currency are per business. English and full Arabic RTL use the same meaning and hierarchy. Internal projects do not require a customer. HR, payroll, production, bookings, rentals and advanced accounting are excluded.",
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "fontFamily": "$md-font",
          "fontSize": 16,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "rohPL",
          "name": "Expanded task routes",
          "fill": "$md-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Purchase 01 Create PO → Order review → 02 Confirmed → 03 Receive items → 04 Supplier invoice → Invoice recorded → Money Pay supplier form → 05 Payment recorded.\nMoney 01 Receive payment → Collection review → 02 Collection recorded. A second ILS 120 receipt on SI-1042 raises paid total from 120 to 240 and leaves 80 due.\nInventory 02 Move stock → 03 Review transfer → 04 Transfer complete. Counts and damage use distinct forms.\nProjects 01 Garden installation → 02 Materials and supply → 03 Review site delivery → 04 Site materials → 05 Usage recorded → 06 Return posted. Buy missing 4 opens Shortfall purchase PO-2049.\nMoney 04 Expense form → 05 Review expense → 06 Expense recorded. Expense ILS 36.50 is paid from Main cash.",
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "fontFamily": "$md-font",
          "fontSize": 16,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "o94Lt",
          "name": "Verification and next work",
          "fill": "$md-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Rendered core, expanded flows, desktop, small-phone and RTL examples. Independent review findings fixed: visible Back controls and business switching. Structural bounds have floating-point and disabled-descendant false positives; screenshots and actual parent bottom extents were checked.\nRemaining: clickable prototype wiring when supported, full Arabic localization of expanded modules, further device/platform variants, receipt/share export behavior, screen-reader and keyboard testing in implementation, and ERPNext deployment/mapping.",
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "fontFamily": "$md-font",
          "fontSize": 16,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "RgnFA",
          "name": "Finalized record navigation",
          "fill": "$md-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "After confirmation, close the task and route Back to its detail/list. Never preserve a finalized form for resubmission. Existing supplier invoice links open Confirmed invoice detail with 100 paid / 170 due; they never reopen Record supplier invoice. After collection, SI-1042 shows paid240 / due80 and both linked payment records.",
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "fontFamily": "$md-font",
          "fontSize": 16,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "PmMAr",
          "name": "Current document inventory",
          "fill": "$md-primary",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "86 editable screen frames · 32 reusable components and state patterns · Mobile 390 px, small phone 320 px, desktop 1440 px, tablet 1024 px · Arabic RTL Home and sale review.",
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "fontFamily": "$md-font",
          "fontSize": 16,
          "fontWeight": "600"
        }
      ]
    },
